    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><ul><li>142 bpm, F# minor. flip a choir sample, pitch down 3 semitones, 808 glides between F# and C#.</li><li>lo-fi thing at 84 bpm: dusty rhodes chords (Fmaj7 - Em7 - Dm7 - Cmaj7), swing the hats 58%.</li><li>try Gross Beat "half speed" on the last bar before the drop instead of a riser.</li><li>drums: layer a clap with a rim on the 2 and 4, short reverb only on the clap.</li><li>the melody I hummed walking back from the lab: 4 notes, D - F - A - G, repeat with the last note up an octave. record it into a voice memo before I forget (did, 10/22).</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Mixing note to self: stop mastering while producing. Fruity Limiter off until the arrangement is done.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
</en-export>
